!********************************************************************** 
!   System:                     H3Cl
!   Functional form:            permutationally invariant polynomial neural network
!   Common name:                H3Cl
!   Number of derivatives:      0
!   Number of bodies:           4
!   Number of electronic surfaces: 1
!   Interface: Section-2
!**********************************************************************
!
!   References: Q. Yao, M. Morita, C. Xie, N. Balakrishnan, and H. Guo
!   "Globally Accurate Full-Dimensional Potential Energy Surface for
!   H2 + HCl Inelastic Scattering"
!   J. Phys. Chem. A 2019, 123, 6578
!
!   Notes: see below
!
!**********************************************************************

**************************************************************
*     H2 + HCl --> H2 + HCl inelastic scattering reaction    *
*     2019.1.20  Qian Yao  updated                           *
*     J. Phys. Chem. A 2019, 123, 6578                       *
**************************************************************
The energies are relative to H2+HCl            
                            
 1)Initialization
   call pes_init

 2) PES obtained by pip-NN fitting and long range fitting
   call pesh3cl(x,vtot)
   x: xyz format geometry in Angstrom
   vtot: potential energy in eV


Description of files

H2.dat  		Bond distances(ang) and ab initio energies(hartree) for H2 

HCl.dat 		Bond distances(ang) and ab initio energies(hartree) for HCl

test.f   		An example FORTRAN program

c.dat                   Fitting Parameters for the long-range potential


1D PESs for H2 and HCl are recommended to obtain by the 6D PES with the r3 at 20 angstrom 
for the PES of H2: only r1 is a variable, fixed other parameters(r2=1.28ang r3=20ang th1=90degree  th2=90degree phi=90degree)
for the PES of HCl: only r2 is a variable, fixed other parameters(r1=0.74ang r3=20ang th1=90degree  th2=90degree phi=90degree)